    "note": "sourceBase and observedAtHead bind the immediately preceding source, test, document and qualification-topology candidate. This implementation-map-only rebind records actual Git objects, not execution success. The normal combined local-plus-federated model-input path admits the current V4 attachment schema, carries partial_peers into compact evidence and retains revoke-before-physical-send fencing. Pull requests have one required qualification owner through blocking-ci while direct branch pushes, workflow_call and workflow_dispatch retain exact-head execution. The authenticated cross-host bridge accepts transport identity only through an issuer/verifier capability bound to the actual local wire owner. HMAC evidence binds local owner, remote peer, profile, channel binding, lifetime, context-key identity and generation; wrong key, wrong profile and wrong-local-host contexts are rejected before replay or attempt state is consumed, and regression tests prove the same request remains admissible through the correct issuer. The stale product atomicity test was migrated off the removed public constructor. The attestation payload is now encoded by the private context itself, so issuance and verification cannot drift through separate argument lists and strict lint does not require a too-many-arguments waiver. The selected network transport, per-host context-key operations, production recovery backend, Agentd serving composition, two-real-host faults/SLOs, independent acceptance and activation/release remain separately gated. The existing V2 product path, authority ownership, no-blind-retry rule and half-budget read reservation are unchanged.",
